 "title": "Hand of Straights",
 "slug": "hand-of-straights",
 "category": "greedy",
 "difficulty": "Medium",
 "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/hand-of-straights/",
 "pattern": "Greedy: the smallest card must start a group",
 "statement": "Given a hand of cards (integers) and a group size `W`, return `True` if the cards can be rearranged into groups of exactly `W` **consecutive** values.",
 "example": {
  "input": "hand = [1,2,3,6,2,3,4,7,8], W = 3",
  "output": "True",
  "why": "[1, 2, 3], [2, 3, 4] and [6, 7, 8]."
 },
 "more": [
  {
   "input": "hand = [1,2,3,4,5], W = 4",
   "output": "False"
  },
  {
   "input": "hand = [1,2,3,4,5,6], W = 2",
   "output": "True"
  },
  {
   "input": "hand = [1,1,2,2,3,3], W = 3",
   "output": "True"
  },
  {
   "input": "hand = [1,2,4], W = 3",
   "output": "False"
  },
  {
   "input": "hand = [8,10,12], W = 3",
   "output": "False"
  },
  {
   "input": "hand = [5], W = 1",
   "output": "True"
  }
 ],
 "idea": [
  "Look at the **smallest** card that is still unused. Nothing smaller exists, so it cannot sit in the middle or at the end of a group — it must be the **start** of one.",
  "So the group is forced: starting at that card `c`, it needs `c, c + 1, …, c + W − 1`. Take one of each from the counts; if any is missing, the hand cannot be arranged.",
  "Repeat with the next smallest unused card until every card is used."
 ],
 "code": "from collections import Counter\n\nclass Solution:\n    def isNStraightHand(self, hand: List[int], W: int) -> bool:\n        if len(hand) % W != 0:\n            return False\n\n        counter = Counter(hand)\n        hand.sort()\n\n        for card in hand:\n            if counter[card] > 0:\n                for i in range(W):\n                    if counter[card + i] <= 0:\n                        return False\n                    counter[card + i] -= 1\n\n        return True",
 "complexity": {
  "time": "O(n log n)",
  "timeWhy": "Sorting dominates; afterwards every card is taken from the counter exactly once.",
  "space": "O(n)",
  "spaceWhy": "The counter holds one entry per distinct card value."
 },
